        <div class="ex-panel" id="cx-data" hidden data-augmented-ui="tl-clip br-clip border">
          <h4>Datasets</h4>
          <p>All of the most common datasets target C/C++ code, and all are at either the function or slice level of granularity. Big-Vul is the only dataset in the top nine to provide labels at more than one granularity, including both function-level and line-level annotations. Furthermore, two of the most widely used datasets (Devign/CodeXGLUE and ReVeal) do not provide CWE-IDs, which may directly contribute to the predominance of binary classification in the literature.</p>
